From bffe9dcf8fb6848d4bde7c232007d1b79d05e4f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 20:35:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02178/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE F0 (INFRA
 safety net; defense-in-depth; fixes BOTH .397 harness bugs) -- (1) add a
 DEGENERATE_CONTROLS check to scripts/adversarial_verify.py + (2) a reusable
 aggregate-available-report-gaps capstone helper. BUG 1: .397's in-generation
 run (exp4293) reported a moat off three bit-identical no-op controls
 (condition_accuracy {{carnot 0.867, rfg 0.3, unguided 0.3, entrgi 0.3}});
 adversarial_verify caught it only via the generic TAUTOLOGY check on the two
 deltas, NOT via a controls-map check. Add a DEGENERATE_CONTROLS check: flag
 CRITICAL when >=2 distinct control arms in a condition_accuracy/arms map are
 bit-identical (the no-op signature) -- the sibling of the .397
 DEGENERATE_SEPARATION check. BUG 2: the .397 capstone (exp4301) + hygiene
 (exp4299) BLOCKED spuriously -- ONE missing artifact (exp4294) hard-blocked
 the whole aggregation and defaulted ALL booleans to False, zeroing out the
 CONCLUSIVE cross-generator verdict (audit:
 docs/research-notes/exp4301-capstone-blocked-spurious-false-2026-06-16.md).
 Build a reusable aggregate-available-report-gaps helper: aggregate the
 artifacts that ARE present, report missing ones as per-axis gaps, and NEVER
 let a missing artifact for one axis zero out a conclusive verdict on another.
 Deliverable = the patched linter + the helper + passing unit tests. Do NOT
 modify scripts/research_conductor.py.

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
---
 ops/changelog.md | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

