 - 2026-06-16: PHASE C1 (BROADEN the selection moat to cross-DOMAIN; the .397 SOTA-ingestion flag; new axis) -- a domain router + per-domain set-encoder that generalizes selection to a HELD-OUT DOMAIN. .397 CLOSED the cross-GENERATOR axis (exp4291 +0.50) -- but the moat is proven only WITHIN ARC, and the verifier is math-domain-bound (math strong, code weak, facts earned-negative). The .397 SOTA ingestion (exp4298) flagged: now that same-substrate cross-generator closed, BROADEN to cross-DOMAIN. Build a router over >=3 domains (ARC families + ARC-GEN generators [reuse exp4291's non-degenerate pool] + FoVer-step/math selection), train ONLY on train-DOMAIN outcomes, test beats-vote on a HELD-OUT DOMAIN frozen (EEVEE interleaved router-prompt co-evolution arXiv:2606.11182; DG-PRM multi-dimensional discriminators arXiv:2507.17849 = the selector-side route to OOD generalization). CRITICAL anti-leak (EEVEE's abstract does not detail leak prevention): a LABEL-ABLATION arm -- the router sees ONLY task features vs sees the domain/family label -- proving it is not just reading domain identity. Non-degenerate guards (vote@1>0.05, oracle<1.0, delta<0.95) so the new adversarial_verify DEGENERATE_SEPARATION check does not fire. Emit cross_domain_selection_holds BARE bool := (held-out-domain delta>0 AND CI95-excl-0 AND non-degenerate guards AND label_ablation_robust). verifier_is_oracle=false. A held-out-domain win is the strongest selection result yet (escapes the domain bound); a collapse is a genuine, decision-grade scope boundary. HARD-CAP to the window; an honest partial (>=3 domains, >=1 held-out, >=~12 held-out tasks) is fine. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: cross_domain_selection_collapses_domain_bound; results/experiment_4305_cross_domain_selector_generalization.json
 - 2026-06-16: PHASE D1 (CONTINUOUS SELF-LEARNING -- the mandated self-learning experiment; harden .397) -- online verifier-weight adaptation with a POWERED CI in the cross-domain regime. research-program.md mandates >=1 self-learning experiment/milestone (Tier-1 = online counter updates, CPU, <1us/update). .397 (exp4295) showed online adaptation HELPS (online_cross_family_delta 0.483 > static 0.417, +0.067; tier-2 fixed: memory 0.428, retrieval 0.456) -- but reported the deltas WITHOUT a powered CI, so 'helps' is not yet decision-grade. HARDEN: re-run Tier-1 online reweighting + Tier-2 RETRIEVAL-augmented selector-context (Decocted 2604.04373 / Dynamic Cheatsheet 2504.07952: retrieval-only CURATED context, NO weight mutation, NO LoRA) across the CROSS-DOMAIN family set (the .395 + exp4291 + the cross-domain pools, a soft input from exp4305) where distribution shift is larger -- and report a POWERED bootstrap CI95 (>=2000 resamples) on (best-adaptive - static). Emit online_adaptation_helps BARE bool := (best-adaptive - static > 0 AND CI95-excl-0). verifier_is_oracle=false. NO fine-tuning; NO TRM; NO live-LoRA. A powered null (static is genuinely the ceiling, CI includes 0) RETIRES the online-adaptation ask (retire_if_same_verdict). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: powered_cross_domain_online_adaptation_helps; results/experiment_4306_self_learning_powered_ci_cross_domain.json
 - 2026-06-16: PHASE E1 (ARC north star; accuracy) -- monotonic ARC +1 on a NEW game (total_levels >= 23). .397 advanced r11l to L1 (22 levels); .396 ls20; .395 wa30; .394 walled on sc25 L6. Per ARC-AGI-3 Incremental-Progress Scoping (+1, NOT all-levels) + Failed-Experiment Rerun Discipline (a NEW game, not a re-run): target the best-headroom UNATTEMPTED game from the 25-game survey (NOT r11l, NOT ls20, NOT wa30, NOT sc25), with the hardened set-encoder routing the offline solver's candidate ranking. Advance ONE game by >=1 NEW real-env-confirmed level (total_levels 22 -> >=23). Report total_levels + the game advanced + levels_completed (from the solver's real-env-confirmed output, not a self-report). NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission. An honest no-advance is COMPLETE and informs the next game pick. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: incremental_progress_no_advance_re86-8af5384d_L1_selected_frontier_adapter_unavailable; results/experiment_4307_arc_incremental_progress_new_game.json
